-- title:
--   Acceptance effect of the physical coherent-certificate verifier
-- statement:
--   For every G₂ verifier V, the compiled verifier’s acceptance operator is I minus the direct sum of certificate rejection effects, transported along the proof-basis bijection. Valid claims have rejection D†D for the selected block D; invalid claims have rejection I.
--
--   $$
--   (E_{V^{\prime}})_{x,y}=\left(I-\bigoplus_cR_c\right)_{\varphi(x),\varphi(y)}.
--   $$
--
--   Here the basis bijection identifies physical proof bits with history and claim coordinates. The formula transfers the block rejection analysis to the actual verifier.
